    {
      "gridPos": {
        "h": 10,
        "w": 24,
        "x": 0,
        "y": 36
      },
      "id": 5,
      "options": {
        "content": "### Create-lead - the bottleneck  (latency / scaling risk, 0 failures)\n- **Risk** - create() p95 = **15.1 s** at 100 concurrent users (**75%** of the 20 s gate); scales **~5.5x** from 10 -> 100 users, so ~130-140 concurrent creates would breach the gate. Lead intake is the first thing to buckle under a spike.\n- **Cause** - create() is **serialized**, not compute-bound: latency grows with *concurrency* (requests queue), not payload - the signature of a shared serial resource (Odoo's synchronous lead assignment / scoring + row locks on each new lead).\n- **Evidence** - on the *same* new leads, a `search` returns in **0.68 s** avg but a `delete` (`unlink`) **blocks up to 121 s** (avg **62.7 s**, p95 **92 s**). Fast read + stalled write on identical rows = they are **lock-held by the assignment cron** - the same contention that inflates create() under load. (Deletes are cleanup-only, so they never fail the test - but they are the clearest fingerprint of the lock.)\n\n### Login - healthy\np95 stays **< 1 s** even at 100 users and scales **sub-linearly** (2.2x for a 10x user increase). Heavier half is the initial `GET /web/login` CSRF page (p95 1.14 s) vs the auth `POST` (0.95 s) - a static-asset detail, not a scaling concern.\n\n_Baseline: login #2, create-lead #6. All requests succeeded - this is a latency/scaling risk, not a functional defect. Watch create() p95 @ 100u build-over-build._",
        "mode": "markdown"
      },
      "title": "Bottleneck diagnosis - risk / cause / evidence",
      "type": "text"
    },
